"program_narrative": "Program ERRHNDL is an online (CICS) centralized error handler, invoked by EXEC CICS LINK from DB2RECV and INQONLN with the ERRHND error block as COMMAREA. It copies the COMMAREA into working storage, stamps the error with the current date and time, and generates a trace ID from FUNCTION RANDOM when none was supplied. It then copies the error fields into a host-variable record and inserts one row into the DB2 table ERRLOG; if the insert fails it replaces the message with 'Error logging failed' and marks the error fatal. Next it rebuilds the message as 'Error in <program> - <message> (<trace id>)'. Finally it sets the recovery action from the severity: fatal errors request an abend ('A'), warnings and informational errors request continuation ('C'), and any other severity requests a return ('R'). The updated error block is copied back to the COMMAREA and the program ends with EXEC CICS RETURN.",
